1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:06,694
A typhoon is coming soon.

2
00:00:06,778 --> 00:00:08,863
Because of it, a landslide will occur.

3
00:00:08,947 --> 00:00:12,367
Those five you are
so close with will all die.

4
00:00:15,036 --> 00:00:16,663
Mr. Nishigami?

5
00:00:16,746 --> 00:00:20,125
Let me tell you what will happen
if you break the code.

6
00:00:20,208 --> 00:00:21,668
Every human involved with you

7
00:00:21,751 --> 00:00:25,046
will have all Grim Reaper
related memories erased.

8
00:00:25,129 --> 00:00:26,089
And of course,

9
00:00:26,172 --> 00:00:30,009
you yourself will be punished
by the laws of the underworld.

10
00:00:30,093 --> 00:00:31,427
Such a thing is impossible!

11
00:00:31,511 --> 00:00:34,097
The typhoon passes through multiple areas.

12
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:35,473
Up on that mountain,

13
00:00:35,557 --> 00:00:37,600
there is an old shrine nobody visits.

14
00:00:37,684 --> 00:00:42,105
All natural disasters around here
are governed by that shrine.

15
00:00:42,188 --> 00:00:45,900
If you go there, you may
be able to change something.

16
00:00:47,861 --> 00:00:50,321
A Grim Reaper in human form?

17
00:00:50,405 --> 00:00:52,323
A Grim Reaper…

18
00:00:52,407 --> 00:00:53,908
Are you here to collect me?

19
00:00:53,992 --> 00:00:55,326
I'm sorry.

20
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:57,537
I can't die. Yeah.

21
00:00:58,204 --> 00:01:00,915
Because I'm a god.

22
00:01:05,879 --> 00:01:09,674
Well now, what do you need from me today?

23
00:01:11,259 --> 00:01:12,427
Who are you?

24
00:01:14,804 --> 00:01:17,599
Japan is home to myriad gods,

25
00:01:17,682 --> 00:01:22,812
and their origins trace back
to the nature worship of the Jomon period.

26
00:01:22,896 --> 00:01:27,734
As for me, the wind, water,
clouds, rain, lightning…

27
00:01:29,027 --> 00:01:31,946
I control all weather!

28
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:34,532
I am an ancient god of Japan!

29
00:01:34,616 --> 00:01:37,243
The venerable Dragon God!

30
00:01:37,327 --> 00:01:39,996
DRAGON GOD

31
00:01:41,831 --> 00:01:43,124
Dragon God.

32
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:45,460
Yes, well…

33
00:01:46,127 --> 00:01:47,378
That aside,

34
00:01:47,462 --> 00:01:52,133
what is a handsome young Reaper
like you doing here in the mountains…

35
00:01:52,217 --> 00:01:53,468
Oh, right.

36
00:01:53,551 --> 00:01:56,471
There's a typhoon today, right?
You must be busy too.

37
00:01:59,057 --> 00:02:02,101
I am sorry for the sudden visit.

38
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:06,022
I need to ask you a favor.

39
00:02:06,773 --> 00:02:07,815
Okay.

40
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:11,861
Then, shall I at least hear you out?

41
00:02:11,945 --> 00:02:13,196
What is it?

42
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:16,324
The landslide.

43
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:22,247
I want you to prevent it.

44
00:02:24,374 --> 00:02:25,333
What?

45
00:02:26,709 --> 00:02:27,710
Why?

46
00:02:29,379 --> 00:02:32,048
There are humans I want to save.

47
00:02:33,049 --> 00:02:34,842
Oh, I see.

48
00:02:34,926 --> 00:02:35,885
Huh…

49
00:02:36,511 --> 00:02:41,641
So those people are fated to die
in tonight's landslide?

50
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:43,351
Yes.

51
00:02:44,227 --> 00:02:48,106
Five young humans
have been marked for death.

52
00:02:49,023 --> 00:02:51,067
Those people haven't…

53
00:02:52,068 --> 00:02:53,152
done much.

54
00:02:54,779 --> 00:02:56,030
Really…

55
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:02,662
They haven't achieved anything at all.

56
00:03:02,745 --> 00:03:03,705
But this summer…

57
00:03:06,916 --> 00:03:08,376
many things happened…

58
00:03:10,086 --> 00:03:11,671
at that villa.

59
00:03:15,049 --> 00:03:16,426
I think,

60
00:03:17,802 --> 00:03:19,512
throughout this vacation…

61
00:03:21,806 --> 00:03:23,725
they all discovered something.

62
00:03:36,654 --> 00:03:40,533
"I want to protect
those young people's future."

63
00:03:40,616 --> 00:03:44,245
I guess that's what
you're trying to say, but…

64
00:03:44,871 --> 00:03:48,416
That isn't something
a Grim Reaper should say.

65
00:03:49,709 --> 00:03:51,502
But, I…

66
00:03:53,171 --> 00:03:54,297
Look.

67
00:03:55,089 --> 00:03:57,717
Today, without a doubt,
a landslide will occur.

68
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,720
You cannot change that absolute fact.

69
00:04:01,679 --> 00:04:06,768
However, there is a place
that is safe from that disaster.

70
00:04:06,851 --> 00:04:08,353
And I know where it is.

71
00:04:09,228 --> 00:04:10,813
It's right here.

72
00:04:11,814 --> 00:04:16,152
Hundreds of years ago,
humans built a shrine here

73
00:04:16,235 --> 00:04:18,488
because it was a safe place.

74
00:04:18,571 --> 00:04:21,491
Rain pours down hard
on the top of this mountain.

75
00:04:21,574 --> 00:04:23,868
Then the flood comes rushing down.

76
00:04:23,951 --> 00:04:24,911
However,

77
00:04:25,495 --> 00:04:30,416
the water that comes out of the valley
above here splits into two directions.

78
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,459
And, what's more…

79
00:04:32,001 --> 00:04:34,212
Look around here. It's all bamboo.

80
00:04:34,295 --> 00:04:35,755
There is a bamboo grove.

81
00:04:36,798 --> 00:04:39,133
It protects the ground.

82
00:04:39,217 --> 00:04:42,637
They say bamboo roots
are all connected underground,

83
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,596
like a net.

84
00:04:43,679 --> 00:04:49,769
So, this place is right on top
of a natural safety net.

85
00:04:52,772 --> 00:04:53,856
Then…

86
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,526
Yes, exactly.

87
00:04:57,151 --> 00:05:01,447
If you bring the humans here
before the landslide happens,

88
00:05:01,531 --> 00:05:02,865
they will all survive.

89
00:05:03,866 --> 00:05:05,159
Hey there!

90
00:05:05,243 --> 00:05:06,369
Wait a minute.

91
00:05:07,078 --> 00:05:08,287
Hey.

92
00:05:09,038 --> 00:05:10,957
You're a Grim Reaper, right?

93
00:05:11,707 --> 00:05:14,377
Are you sure you should be doing this?

94
00:05:17,338 --> 00:05:18,381
It's fine.

95
00:05:19,132 --> 00:05:20,383
I have already…

96
00:05:22,468 --> 00:05:23,719
worked enough.

97
00:06:10,224 --> 00:06:14,353
As expected, the calm earlier on the shore
was the calm before the storm.

98
00:06:14,437 --> 00:06:16,355
It is very windy here now!

99
00:06:16,439 --> 00:06:20,067
-Do not go outside during this storm!
-It sounds real bad!

100
00:06:20,151 --> 00:06:22,445
-It's impressive.
-Please seek shelter inside!

101
00:06:22,528 --> 00:06:24,322
The wind is getting stronger.

102
00:06:24,405 --> 00:06:26,407
Yeah. It will be okay, right?

103
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:28,618
This house won't get blown away, right?

104
00:06:28,701 --> 00:06:31,078
I think it's quite well built.

105
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:35,208
Just in case there's a blackout,
we have a flashlight!

106
00:06:35,291 --> 00:06:39,337
But when its battery runs out,
let's kiss again, Rinrin!

107
00:06:40,713 --> 00:06:43,007
-We have this lamp too.
-Oh, nice!

108
00:06:43,633 --> 00:06:45,885
Camping stuff is so useful
for times like this.

109
00:06:45,968 --> 00:06:48,095
I should charge my phone now!

110
00:06:48,179 --> 00:06:49,347
Rinrin, here.

111
00:06:50,139 --> 00:06:53,434
I should also move the stuff
in the fridge to the cooler.

112
00:06:53,517 --> 00:06:55,269
I'll go check a few things.

113
00:07:00,107 --> 00:07:01,400
We've got a problem!

114
00:07:01,484 --> 00:07:02,401
What is it?

115
00:07:02,902 --> 00:07:05,154
I just noticed we have quite a leak here!

116
00:07:05,238 --> 00:07:07,698
-A leak? Wait a minute.
-Yeah.

117
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:09,951
Use these.

118
00:07:10,034 --> 00:07:11,911
Yeah, okay.

119
00:07:22,004 --> 00:07:23,464
Mr. Nishigami?

120
00:07:24,632 --> 00:07:26,884
Everyone, let's get out of here.

121
00:07:31,097 --> 00:07:33,099
We are going out in this weather?

122
00:07:33,182 --> 00:07:35,226
-It's dangerous to stay here.
-Oh, no!

123
00:07:35,309 --> 00:07:36,143
Rinrin, you okay?

124
00:07:36,227 --> 00:07:38,604
-I can't get them on.
-Oh, I'm so wet!

125
00:07:38,688 --> 00:07:41,065
They are hard to put on!

126
00:07:41,148 --> 00:07:43,317
-The oranges!
-Hurry up!

127
00:07:43,901 --> 00:07:47,780
The velcro… the velcro's not sticking!

128
00:07:51,492 --> 00:07:53,327
They're being blown away!

129
00:08:22,982 --> 00:08:24,275
Mr. Nishigami.

130
00:08:24,859 --> 00:08:27,194
What are you doing? It's dangerous here.

131
00:08:28,446 --> 00:08:30,573
What if something happens to you?

132
00:08:31,574 --> 00:08:32,700
Mr. Nishigami!

133
00:08:33,284 --> 00:08:35,244
Please, help me pick the oranges.

134
00:09:17,328 --> 00:09:18,412
I…

135
00:09:20,915 --> 00:09:22,583
have met you before.

136
00:09:24,502 --> 00:09:25,544
Thank you.

137
00:09:36,430 --> 00:09:37,515
Come on.

138
00:09:38,099 --> 00:09:39,392
This place isn't safe.

139
00:09:39,934 --> 00:09:40,935
Let's go.

140
00:09:48,734 --> 00:09:49,819
Jeez…

141
00:09:50,319 --> 00:09:53,864
He really went and did it.

142
00:10:08,379 --> 00:10:11,799
This is going to turn into quite a storm.

143
00:10:13,634 --> 00:10:15,845
No matter how much AI evolves,

144
00:10:15,928 --> 00:10:17,930
it can't stop a typhoon.
Isn't it powerless?

145
00:10:19,098 --> 00:10:22,393
This storm really
makes you feel the limits of AI.

146
00:10:22,977 --> 00:10:24,937
I wonder if that villa is okay?

147
00:10:26,605 --> 00:10:28,566
A direct hit on Tatsumi Town?

148
00:10:29,817 --> 00:10:32,903
That villa was built
on a slope facing the sea.

149
00:10:35,406 --> 00:10:36,991
I hope it isn't damaged.

150
00:10:57,970 --> 00:11:03,851
DISASTER PREVENTION COMMITTEE

151
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:17,156
Oh, no! I'm soaked!

152
00:11:17,239 --> 00:11:19,658
-Be careful! The rain is really pouring!
-I'm cold!

153
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:21,410
Everyone, get inside.

154
00:11:22,203 --> 00:11:23,787
Tsumugi, hurry!

155
00:11:23,871 --> 00:11:25,748
I thought I was going to die!

156
00:11:26,832 --> 00:11:29,293
-Wow!
-It's safe here.

157
00:11:30,252 --> 00:11:31,504
My grandma's ashes.

158
00:11:31,587 --> 00:11:34,924
It's fine. We'll go back there
once the typhoon passes.

159
00:11:37,885 --> 00:11:38,719
But…

160
00:11:39,261 --> 00:11:41,972
I feel like I shouldn't leave them there.

161
00:11:44,058 --> 00:11:45,100
I'll go get them.

162
00:11:45,768 --> 00:11:46,727
What?

163
00:11:49,855 --> 00:11:50,856
Mr. Nishigami!

164
00:11:51,899 --> 00:11:53,275
It's raining hard.

165
00:11:53,359 --> 00:11:55,611
Are you going down
that mountain path again?

166
00:11:58,030 --> 00:11:59,114
Why…

167
00:12:01,283 --> 00:12:05,329
Why do so much for me?

168
00:12:11,085 --> 00:12:12,169
I…

169
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:15,047
have met you before.

170
00:12:20,719 --> 00:12:21,929
Who are you?

171
00:12:35,359 --> 00:12:36,527
Ms. Midori.

172
00:12:37,945 --> 00:12:39,280
This summer

173
00:12:40,239 --> 00:12:42,241
was the best vacation.

174
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:43,993
Thank you.

175
00:12:48,664 --> 00:12:49,665
I…

176
00:12:52,876 --> 00:12:54,378
I like you,

177
00:12:55,754 --> 00:12:56,839
Mr. Nishigami.

178
00:12:59,925 --> 00:13:01,051
Me too.

179
00:13:02,845 --> 00:13:04,722
I like you, Ms. Midori.

180
00:13:06,098 --> 00:13:07,683
And I probably will…

181
00:13:10,019 --> 00:13:11,061
forever.

182
00:13:48,641 --> 00:13:49,600
Goodbye.

183
00:14:00,444 --> 00:14:01,612
Mr. Nishigami…

184
00:14:34,019 --> 00:14:35,396
You came

185
00:14:36,939 --> 00:14:39,024
to save me too, didn't you?

186
00:14:40,693 --> 00:14:41,652
Yes.

187
00:14:42,736 --> 00:14:45,364
Sorry for forgetting you.

188
00:14:49,410 --> 00:14:52,037
Thank you, Mr. Nishigami.

189
00:14:53,288 --> 00:14:56,458
For saving those children.

190
00:15:03,966 --> 00:15:07,970
A Grim Reaper, saving humans…

191
00:15:14,768 --> 00:15:17,813
It's the opposite
of what I should be doing.

192
00:15:23,944 --> 00:15:25,279
But I feel like

193
00:15:26,447 --> 00:15:32,619
the reason I kept being a Reaper
was to save them someday.

194
00:15:36,331 --> 00:15:39,084
You gave them a second chance at life.

195
00:15:39,835 --> 00:15:45,591
I'm sure they will do their best
to not waste it.

196
00:15:56,393 --> 00:15:59,396
Goodbye, Mr. Nishigami!

197
00:16:16,747 --> 00:16:18,707
The best vacation…

198
00:16:32,971 --> 00:16:34,139
Thank you…

199
00:16:35,724 --> 00:16:36,809
everyone.

200
00:17:25,983 --> 00:17:26,859
What?

201
00:17:27,484 --> 00:17:28,777
We…

202
00:17:31,321 --> 00:17:33,448
You've done something terrible.

203
00:17:33,532 --> 00:17:35,909
I erased those humans' memories.

204
00:17:35,993 --> 00:17:37,911
Is this where the villa was?

205
00:17:37,995 --> 00:17:39,496
The villa is gone!

206
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:42,040
No one remembers you anymore.

207
00:17:42,624 --> 00:17:46,128
Is God telling us
that our vacation is over?

208
00:17:47,379 --> 00:17:49,089
Why did it come to this?

209
00:17:49,673 --> 00:17:53,844
Your human form has become grains of sand,
turned into sea foam,

210
00:17:55,179 --> 00:17:56,680
and vanished.

211
00:17:58,056 --> 00:17:59,016
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

